@title Kitting: bought bars say to buy, rows read cleanly, and the pick list numbers are explained
@area Reports
# Reports > Bench output > Kitting: the bar rows of the Prepare pick list say "New bar, to buy" (not Stock) and carry no stray semicolon; a line explains that pick list numbers follow the assembly checklist, so step 2 (Drill) has none.
open qa/fixtures/cabinet-cooling-advice.novo
wait 30
click_text Reports
wait 5
click_text "Bench output..."
wait 20
click_text Kitting
wait 10
expect "Pick lists keep the step numbers"
expect "New bar, to buy"
expect_not "Stock;"
shot kitting-pick-lists
check_layout
